the winter olympics are right around the  corner here are five things you need to  know  [Music]  number one the sports there are seven  new events at beijing 2022 women's  monobab big air freestyle skiing mixed  teams and short track speed skating  relay ski jumping freestyle ski aerials  and snowboard cross maybe you've caught  on but there are more mixed events  that's how the ioc is promoting greater  gender diversity number two robots lots  and lots of them at the main press  center food is prepared and served by  robot chefs and the dishes get delivered  to tables from an overhead grid to  mitigate the spread of cobid we can  expect to see way more in action there's  a logistics robot for contactless  deliveries and of course virus fighting  robots that roam around with  disinfectant number three the boycott  you may have heard about it the u.s uk  australia canada and denmark are among  the countries staging a diplomatic  boycott over concerns about china's poor  human rights record that means they  won't be sending any political delegates  to beijing but athletes will still  compete in one of the biggest sporting  events in the world  number four the bubble aka the  battleground between china's zero covid  policy and the infectious omicron  variant the closed loop will cover  stadiums venues accommodations and  ceremonies all to keep distance away  from the public and the internet well  within the loop beijing has promised  access to partially unrestricted  internet access dropping the great  firewall that normally blocks services  like facebook and youtube number five  last but not least the athletes from  legends like shaun white uzuru hanyu and  chloe kim to up and coming stars like  eileen goo and matt bae mishkoff they'll  all be there to get their hands on the  gold and hopefully get back home safe  and sound  [Music]
 

